// wrangler.jsonc
//
// Configuration for the Cloudflare Worker that the @astrojs/cloudflare adapter
// builds from this Astro project. The adapter merges this file into the
// generated `dist/server/wrangler.json`.
//
// `name` must match the Worker the store is deployed as, so a deploy updates the
// existing Worker rather than creating a new one.
//
// WHY THERE IS NO `assets` BLOCK HERE
// An earlier attempt to route `<username>.dashpoint.store/` to the storefront
// set `assets.run_worker_first: true`, on the theory that Cloudflare was serving
// the prerendered `/` before the Worker ran. That theory was wrong: the
// short-circuit is INSIDE the Astro entry (`entry.mjs` calls `matchStaticAsset`
// before `app.match`), so `run_worker_first` did not change the outcome and only
// pushed every static asset through the Worker for nothing.
//
// The real fix is `export const prerender = false` in `src/pages/index.astro`:
// with no `dist/client/index.html`, `/` has no static file to short-circuit on,
// so it matches a real route and `src/middleware.ts` runs and can rewrite a
// store subdomain to `/store`. Static assets (`/_astro/*`, `/demo`, ...) are
// still served directly by the edge.
{
    "name": "dashpoint-store",
    "compatibility_date": "2025-01-29"
}
